Z||000010||DaRkLoRD||01-18-2001||03:27 AM||||Just a side note, images should <B>always</B> be resized in a graphics program if you want to display them at a different size... if they're just resized (to be smaller) with HTML code, it still takes the full amount of time to download, plus a bit of CPU time to draw it at the correct resolution.. so, in effect, it takes longer than if it were shown at full size!<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
